{"version_id": 32, "article_id": 4, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Former German spy chief arrested for spying and treason", "title_zh": "德国前情报头子因间谍和叛国罪被捕", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c58jzyer1kr0o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(230, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(268, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "cf9eb2e77a6c"}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 169, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "A former head of Germany's spy agency has been arrested. Police say he passed secret information to other countries.", "lead_zh": "德国情报机构的前负责人被捕了。警方说他把机密情报传给了其他国家。", "preview": "August Hanning used to lead Germany's spy agency, the BND. He worked there from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant.", "preview_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁曾经领导德国情报机构——联邦情报局（BND）。他在1998年到2005年期间在那里工作。之后，他做私人顾问。现在他惹上了法律麻烦。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 22, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@8df5e71/content/audio/4/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 70.688, "size_bytes": 427824, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 193, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@8df5e71/content/data/versions/32.json", "paragraphs": ["August Hanning used to lead Germany's spy agency, the BND. He worked there from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now he is in trouble with the law.", "Prosecutors say Hanning used secret information to write a report for a foreign spy service. They also say he was in contact with another foreign spy service for many years.", "Police also arrested a former BND worker, Manfred D. They say he gave Hanning about 2,000 secret documents. He did this for money. Manfred D was Hanning's office chief and stayed at the BND until this year.", "Police arrested Hanning at his home near Münster. They arrested Manfred D in Bavaria. Hanning will go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D will go to court on Tuesday.", "The case was found during another investigation. That case was about Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress. Police found a storage device with secret BND documents. This is not the first time the BND has had this kind of problem."], "paragraphs_zh": ["奥古斯特·汉宁曾经领导德国情报机构——联邦情报局（BND）。他在1998年到2005年期间在那里工作。之后，他做私人顾问。现在他惹上了法律麻烦。", "检察官说，汉宁利用秘密情报为一个外国间谍机构撰写了一份分析报告。他们还说他多年来一直与另一个外国间谍机构保持联系。", "警方还逮捕了一名BND前员工，曼弗雷德·D。他们说，他给了汉宁大约2000份秘密文件。他这么做是为了钱。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任，直到今年才离开BND。", "警方在明斯特附近汉宁的家中逮捕了他。他们在巴伐利亚逮捕了曼弗雷德·D。汉宁将于周三出庭。曼弗雷德·D将于周二出庭。", "这个案子是在另一起调查中发现的。那起案件与德国牛排连锁店女继承人克里斯蒂娜·布洛克有关。警方发现了一个存储设备，里面有BND的秘密文件。这已经不是BND第一次遇到这类问题了。"], "body": "August Hanning used to lead Germany's spy agency, the BND. He worked there from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now he is in trouble with the law.\n\nProsecutors say Hanning used secret information to write a report for a foreign spy service. They also say he was in contact with another foreign spy service for many years.\n\nPolice also arrested a former BND worker, Manfred D. They say he gave Hanning about 2,000 secret documents. He did this for money. Manfred D was Hanning's office chief and stayed at the BND until this year.\n\nPolice arrested Hanning at his home near Münster. They arrested Manfred D in Bavaria. Hanning will go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D will go to court on Tuesday.\n\nThe case was found during another investigation. That case was about Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress. Police found a storage device with secret BND documents. This is not the first time the BND has had this kind of problem.", "body_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁曾经领导德国情报机构——联邦情报局（BND）。他在1998年到2005年期间在那里工作。之后，他做私人顾问。现在他惹上了法律麻烦。\n\n检察官说，汉宁利用秘密情报为一个外国间谍机构撰写了一份分析报告。他们还说他多年来一直与另一个外国间谍机构保持联系。\n\n警方还逮捕了一名BND前员工，曼弗雷德·D。他们说，他给了汉宁大约2000份秘密文件。他这么做是为了钱。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任，直到今年才离开BND。\n\n警方在明斯特附近汉宁的家中逮捕了他。他们在巴伐利亚逮捕了曼弗雷德·D。汉宁将于周三出庭。曼弗雷德·D将于周二出庭。\n\n这个案子是在另一起调查中发现的。那起案件与德国牛排连锁店女继承人克里斯蒂娜·布洛克有关。警方发现了一个存储设备，里面有BND的秘密文件。这已经不是BND第一次遇到这类问题了。", "text": "August Hanning used to lead Germany's spy agency, the BND. He worked there from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now he is in trouble with the law. Prosecutors say Hanning used secret information to write a report for a foreign spy service. They also say he was in contact with another foreign spy service for many years. Police also arrested a former BND worker, Manfred D. They say he gave Hanning about 2,000 secret documents. He did this for money. Manfred D was Hanning's office chief and stayed at the BND until this year. Police arrested Hanning at his home near Münster. They arrested Manfred D in Bavaria. Hanning will go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D will go to court on Tuesday. The case was found during another investigation. That case was about Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress. Police found a storage device with secret BND documents. This is not the first time the BND has had this kind of problem.", "vocab": [{"word": "spy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "间谍", "note": "指秘密收集情报的人。"}, {"word": "arrest", "pos": "verb", "zh": "逮捕", "note": "常用被动语态：be arrested。"}, {"word": "secret", "pos": "adj", "zh": "秘密的", "note": "可作形容词或名词。"}, {"word": "information", "pos": "noun", "zh": "信息；情报", "note": "不可数名词，不能加s。"}, {"word": "prosecutor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "检察官", "note": "负责起诉的人。"}, {"word": "document", "pos": "noun", "zh": "文件", "note": "指书面或电子文件。"}, {"word": "court", "pos": "noun", "zh": "法庭", "note": "go to court 表示出庭。"}, {"word": "investigation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "调查", "note": "动词是 investigate。"}], "title_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason", "summary_original": "August Hanning is accused of obtaining classified information for a foreign power.", "body_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason\nBy\nOlivia Ireland\nPublished\n6 hours ago\nFormer German spy chief August Hanning has been arrested on suspicion of espionage, treason and obtaining classified information for a foreign power, the German Federal Prosecutor's Office says.\nHanning headed the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005 and has since been working as a private consultant.\nProsecutors allege that he used classified intelligence to \"draft an analysis\" for one foreign intelligence service and maintained contact with another foreign spying service. Investigators have not disclosed which foreign powers were involved.\nPolice also arrested former BND employee Manfred D, accusing him of passing Hanning about 2,000 classified documents for money.\nManfred D, who was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, is charged with aiding and abetting attempted treason and treasonous espionage.\nLocal media reported Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde near Münster while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday and Manfred D will appear on Tuesday.\nProsecutors say Manfred D, who also served as the chief of staff for Hanning's successors between 2012 and 2026, used his role to gain access to highly confidential information which he then passed on to Hanning \"in exchange for remuneration\".\n\"The current findings suggest that, over the years, Manfred D provided Hanning with approximately 2,000 documents, many of which contained classified information to be used exclusively by the Federal Intelligence Service for internal purposes,\" the statement says.\n\"On one occasion, Hanning used classified intelligence ... to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign intelligence service,\" prosecutors said, noting it was not clear if \"the material reached the intended recipient\".\nHanning is also accused of being \"in close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed on political information, partially based on material provided by Manfred D, for several years\".\nLocal media say Hanning's alleged possession of intelligence documents came to light during a separate case relating to German steakhouse heiress Christina Block.\nHamburg public prosecutor's office accused Block of orchestrating the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023 due to a custody dispute. Investigators allege Hanning was involved in an earlier attempted kidnapping of the children, which he denies.\nState criminal police officers reportedly discovered an electronic data storage device containing sensitive information including recent BND documents.\nIt is not the first time the BND has faced similar controversy. A high-ranking German intelligence officer was\ncharged with treason in 2023\nfor allegedly passing state secrets to Russia.\nProsecutors alleged Carsten L shared intelligence about the war in Ukraine and the Wagner mercenary group and received roughly €400,000 ($450,000; £340,000). His trial is ongoing.\nRelated topics\nGermany\nCorruption\nSpying\nMore on this story\nAlmost 60,000 far-right extremists in Germany, intelligence agency says\nPublished\n30 June\nGermany investigates Russia links to weapons cache discovered in woods, reports say\nPublished\n21 August", "fetched_at": "2026-10-06T16:39:02.526512", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "August", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.537, "sm": 100, "em": 537, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Hanning", "s": 0.55, "e": 0.875, "sm": 550, "em": 875, "cs": 7, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "used", "s": 0.887, "e": 1.15, "sm": 887, "em": 1150, "cs": 15, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "to", "s": 1.163, "e": 1.25, "sm": 1162, "em": 1250, "cs": 20, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "lead", "s": 1.262, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1262, "em": 1525, "cs": 23, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Germany's", "s": 1.538, "e": 2.0, "sm": 1537, "em": 2000, "cs": 28, "ce": 37, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "spy", "s": 2.013, "e": 2.312, "sm": 2012, "em": 2312, "cs": 38, "ce": 41, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "agency", "s": 2.325,